#{[17592186357266 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186356815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357266 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c1db56dc-7afb-5c75-8b54-941d34316501" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186355854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357307 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "da01e0af-4eb5-5d89-b320-97ae18e3c7cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357595 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357595 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357595 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357595 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$   Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "689d9753-4018-5be8-9d81-e1a605de8efc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357595 #edb/ref 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =12-8 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357603 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357603 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93968" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357603 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357603 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357603 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e96ec148-dcd3-5736-b705-6d0e6370e151" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357603 #edb/ref 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =18-8-7 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357606 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357606 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357606 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357606 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-2 & 4 \\\\ \\,2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357606 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f0bce3e-c7ad-5cbe-a214-649d56d182b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357606 #edb/ref 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357610 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186356990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357610 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93984" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357610 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357610 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357610 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09763352-7b89-5e95-8516-57e6bce8d181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357610 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357615 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9eb1f202-37a9-5513-9728-465e7c426c0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357615 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357632 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357632 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357632 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357632 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357632 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04f3f719-b108-5208-92b0-9457c6817de3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357632 #edb/ref 1074 "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =(-4){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+\\,\\,3{x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4$ and $b=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=-4+3=-1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357635 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357635 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357635 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357635 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c502fc9-407f-54ee-a63b-8ef283056af2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357635 #edb/ref 1074 "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+(-3)=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423302 #edb/ref 1080 "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423302 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423302 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08e5bf9a-2ab7-5739-b14d-f546e211c130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423303 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423303 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423303 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09004ef9-4917-58d2-8c07-5742c23a3707" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423304 #edb/ref 1080 "4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423304 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423304 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b02a7dc-3d77-54f9-9eab-4104398fd87b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423305 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423305 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423305 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423306 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423306 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423306 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423307 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423307 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423307 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21bd4957-61ca-515f-955c-429ec430a2c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423308 #edb/ref 1080 "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423308 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 175921